the monkey. Brain Res 286:267&#x02013;297 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6189562</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR5"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Asanuma</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Thach</surname><given-names>WT</given-names></name><name><surname>Jones</surname><given-names>EG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Distribution of cerebellar terminations and their relation to other afferent terminations in the ventral lateral thalamic region of the monkey</article-title><source>Brain Res</source><year>1983</year><volume>286</volume><fpage>237</fpage><lpage>265</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Asanuma C, Thach WT, Jones EG (1983b) Distribution of cerebellar terminations and their relation to other afferent terminations in the ventral lateral thalamic region of the monkey. Brain Res 286:237&#x02013;265 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6189561</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Aufenberg</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Sarnthein</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Morel</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Rousson</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Gallay</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Jeanmonod</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A revival of Spiegel&#x02019;s campotomy: long term results of the stereotactic pallidothalamic tractotomy against the parkinsonian thalamocortical dysrhythmia</article-title><source>Thalamus Relat Syst</source><year>2005</year><volume>3</volume><fpage>121</fpage><lpage>132</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1017/S147292880700012X</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Aufenberg C, Sarnthein J, Morel A, Rousson V, Gallay M, Jeanmonod D (